{
  "id": "COMPOUND:11153 - PROTEIN:5848",
  "verbalization": "Propamidine appears to exert its biological effects through a shared target, Oleamide, which is involved in the regulation of Raji cells. The evidence suggests that Propamidine acts as a target of Oleamide, with multiple pathways converging on this interaction. Path_87019 and Path_87020 both indicate that Propamidine targets Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like and Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9, which are both targets of Oleamide, ultimately leading to a reduction in Raji cell activity. Path_87021 further supports this by showing that Oleamide targets (2E,4E)-N-isobutylundeca-2,4-dien-8,10-diynamide, which also affects Raji cells. The consistent presence of Oleamide as a mediator in multiple pathways strengthens the hypothesis that Propamidine and Raji are linked via a common mechanism involving Oleamide. The evidence is robust and suggests a mechanistic link, though the exact nature of the interaction between Propamidine and Oleamide remains to be fully elucidated.",
